1
00:01:58,959 --> 00:02:00,920
Sis, Mom was diagnosed with breast cancer.

2
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,319
The doctor said we must start treatment right away.

3
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:03,480
We're already in the city.

4
00:02:03,480 --> 00:02:04,640
Where exactly do you live?

5
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,360
Sis, you've been gone for over two months.

6
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:11,680
It took Mom calling you

7
00:02:11,680 --> 00:02:13,080
to find out you got a new job.

8
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,800
Yet you haven't sent any money home.

9
00:02:15,319 --> 00:02:16,879
Is Mom not your own mother too?

10
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,879
So you're just dropping the burden of this family on me?

11
00:02:21,599 --> 00:02:22,800
Where are you right now?

12
00:02:32,879 --> 00:02:34,240
It's already in the mid-to-late stage.

13
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,120
We recommend surgery plus a few rounds of chemo.

14
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,759
It's best done at a major hospital in the city.

15
00:02:37,759 --> 00:02:39,199
The facilities there are much better.

16
00:02:40,919 --> 00:02:42,080
About how much will it cost?

17
00:02:42,479 --> 00:02:45,240
The surgery will be around 30,000 to 40,000.

18
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:46,840
And there will be chemotherapy afterward.

19
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:49,520
The drugs can be imported or domestic.

20
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,039
Insurance only covers the domestic ones.

21
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:52,879
As for the rest,

22
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,560
it depends on your family's financial situation.

23
00:02:56,599 --> 00:02:58,120
If it costs that much, I'm not doing it.

24
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,319
Xiaoqiang, come home with me.

25
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,120
No matter what, I'm dying at home.

26
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:01,439
Mom.

27
00:03:01,439 --> 00:03:02,520
Even if I die, I'll die at home.

28
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:03,000
Mom, what are you talking about?

29
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,080
We'll treat it.

30
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,800
How can you just refuse treatment?

31
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,039
The doctor just said

32
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:09,199
we caught it early,

33
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,319
so there's still hope.

34
00:03:10,479 --> 00:03:11,319
How do we treat it?

35
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:13,360
Where do we go?

36
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,639
Where are we going to find that much money?

37
00:03:17,159 --> 00:03:18,400
Your dad is paralyzed at home,

38
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,120
and your brother still doesn't have a job.

39
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:23,639
Didn't I say my fantasy novel went off track?

40
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,800
If I write an infinite flow novel next,

41
00:03:24,919 --> 00:03:25,840
it'll definitely blow up.

42
00:03:26,159 --> 00:03:27,080
Just not right now.

43
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:28,479
Don't worry about the money.

44
00:03:30,240 --> 00:03:32,159
Don't worry, I'm here.

45
00:03:36,159 --> 00:03:37,240
Where's your brother?

46
00:03:39,639 --> 00:03:41,520
He said he's finding a quiet place, cooking up something big.

47
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:42,639
Where is he staying?

48
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,680
I found him a temporary place

49
00:03:46,479 --> 00:03:47,400
and rented it for half a month.

50
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:50,879
I wonder how he's living,

51
00:03:50,879 --> 00:03:51,879
what he's eating.

52
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:58,000
If you have some spare cash,

53
00:03:59,159 --> 00:04:01,080
put your brother up in a hotel.

54
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:04,520
Mom, where would I get spare cash?

55
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,000
I had to borrow money for your surgery.

56
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,680
I borrowed it from Lawyer Zhou.

57
00:04:10,159 --> 00:04:11,080
Lawyer Zhou?

58
00:04:12,479 --> 00:04:13,319
How old is he?

59
00:04:13,319 --> 00:04:14,159
Is he married?

60
00:04:16,279 --> 00:04:17,879
A lawyer wouldn't be a bad match.

61
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,160
If he has time,

62
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:21,519
let me meet him.

63
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,480
Mom, how many times do I have to tell you?

64
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,560
How many times do I have to tell you?

65
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,879
I went there to work!

66
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,519
Did you think I was on a blind date?

67
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,240
I'm earning money to support the whole family.

68
00:04:30,240 --> 00:04:31,079
Can you please stop having

69
00:04:31,079 --> 00:04:32,360
such filthy thoughts?

70
00:04:32,639 --> 00:04:33,680
What do you mean, filthy?

71
00:04:34,519 --> 00:04:35,680
What's so filthy about that?

72
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:39,839
Men and women get married.

73
00:04:39,839 --> 00:04:41,279
Isn't that just the way things are?

74
00:04:42,439 --> 00:04:44,079
After suffering so much all these years,

75
00:04:44,079 --> 00:04:46,000
I just want to see the two of you do well.

76
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,879
Otherwise, your brother

77
00:04:48,399 --> 00:04:50,519
would be at home writing his masterpiece right now.

78
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,279
Now, following me around,

79
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,800
