80
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:57,759
Does he even know how to write?

81
00:04:57,759 --> 00:04:59,279
Every time I see him, he's just playing games.

82
00:04:59,439 --> 00:05:01,000
Oh, so you know everything now?

83
00:05:02,399 --> 00:05:03,680
What your brother wrote,

84
00:05:03,839 --> 00:05:05,000
I've actually read it all.

85
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,480
It's pretty good.

86
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,160
Figure something out,

87
00:05:10,399 --> 00:05:11,800
and get those friends of yours

88
00:05:11,800 --> 00:05:13,560
to publish your brother's work as a book.

89
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,560
Did he even write that?

90
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:16,319
He ripped it off from a platinum author!

91
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:17,800
He's just messing with you,

92
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:18,600
and you actually believe him.

93
00:05:18,879 --> 00:05:20,439
Are you even his sister?

94
00:05:21,079 --> 00:05:22,240
Every time we talk about your brother,

95
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,839
you never have a single nice thing to say.

96
00:05:24,480 --> 00:05:26,000
All writing under the sun is copied anyway.

97
00:05:26,759 --> 00:05:28,279
What if he keeps copying,

98
00:05:28,279 --> 00:05:29,240
